diff --git a/wefit-investors/README.md b/wefit-investors/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..30a62cf9d3864287270311c683698fbc3b33673b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wefit-investors/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# weFit Labs Investor Experience
+
+A single-page Vite + React + TypeScript application showcasing the investor story for weFit Labs. The page highlights sticky social fitness metrics, distribution flywheels, and monetization, with mobile-first responsiveness and Framer Motion animations.
+
+## Getting Started
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run dev
+```
+
+## Available Scripts
+
+- `npm run dev` – Start the Vite development server.
+- `npm run build` – Build the production bundle.
+- `npm run preview` – Preview the production build.
+- `npm run lint` – Run ESLint across the project.
+- `npm run type-check` – Verify TypeScript types.
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+Create a `.env` file if you need to integrate external services:
+
+```
+VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
+VITE_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_ID
+VITE_CALENDAR_BOOKING_URL=https://calendly.com/wefit-investors
+```
+
+## Tech Stack
+
+- **React 19 + TypeScript**
+- **Vite** for bundling
+- **Tailwind CSS** for styling
+- **Framer Motion** for page and micro-interactions
+- **Lucide Icons** for consistent iconography
+- **React Helmet Async** for SEO metadata
+
+## Folder Structure
+
+```
+src/
+├── components/
+│   ├── layout/
+│   ├── sections/
+│   └── ui/
+├── assets/
+├── hooks/
+├── styles/
+└── utils/
+```
+
+Each section component encapsulates a major narrative block (Hero, Metrics, Problem, Solution, Traction, Business Model, Team, Contact) and can be composed or reordered as investor feedback evolves.
